@startuml domain-model
' Sources: docs/design/requirements.md, sections "Domain Entities" and
' "Relationships and Multiplicities", for the classes and relationships.
' tools/models/ (Phase 02) for the attributes and public methods.
' Attributes are private (-) and exposed as read-only @property (+). No setters.
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class CurrencyPair {
  - _name : str
  - _price_data : tuple[tuple[float, float], ...]
  + __init__(name : str, price_data)
  .. read-only properties ..
  + name : str
  + price_data : tuple[tuple[float, float], ...]
  .. methods ..
  + market_structure() : str
}

class TradeSetup {
  - _pair_name : str
  - _direction : str
  - _entry : float
  - _stop_loss : float
  - _take_profit : float
  + __init__(pair_name : str, direction : str, entry : float, stop_loss : float, take_profit : float)
  .. read-only properties ..
  + pair_name : str
  + direction : str
  + entry : float
  + stop_loss : float
  + take_profit : float
  .. methods ..
  + reward_to_risk() : float
}

class BacktestResult {
  - _pair_name : str
  - _test_date : date
  - _setups_tested : int
  - _trade_count : int
  - _win_count : int
  + __init__(pair_name : str, test_date : date, setups_tested : int, trade_count : int, win_count : int)
  .. read-only properties ..
  + pair_name : str
  + test_date : date
  + setups_tested : int
  + trade_count : int
  + win_count : int
  .. methods ..
  + win_rate() : float | None
}

CurrencyPair "1" -- "0..*" TradeSetup : has >
CurrencyPair "1" -- "0..*" BacktestResult : has >
BacktestResult "0..1" -- "0..*" TradeSetup : is based on >

note "All trade setups in a backtest result must belong\nto the same currency pair as that backtest result." as SamePair
SamePair .. BacktestResult

note as AssociationLinks
  The three associations above are linked by pair_name only;
  object references and same-pair check in Phase 03.
end note
AssociationLinks .. CurrencyPair

note as SharedHelpers
  Shared helper functions (module-level, not classes)
  in tools/models/currency_pair.py:
  + validate_pair_name(name) : str
      used by CurrencyPair, TradeSetup, BacktestResult
  + to_price(value, label) : float
      used by CurrencyPair, TradeSetup
end note

note as ValidationRules
  Validation rules (design decisions, not stated in requirements.md).
  Each violation raises ValueError in __init__.
  Pair name: OANDA format AAA_BBB, two different currencies.
  CurrencyPair: at least 2 (high, low) tuple points;
    prices finite numbers > 0; high >= low.
  TradeSetup: direction "buy" or "sell"; prices finite numbers > 0;
    buy: stop loss < entry < take profit (FR2);
    sell: take profit < entry < stop loss (FR2).
  BacktestResult: test_date is a date; counts are whole numbers >= 0;
    win count <= trade count <= setups tested.
end note
@enduml
